{"ex-E201-1":{"number":"1","title":"Photoelectric effect experiment","question":"<p>In the photoelectric effect experiment, the graph of the photoelectric current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mrow><mtext>I</mtext></mrow></mrow></math> against the potential difference <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mrow><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></math> across the photocell is as shown.</p><p>(a) What is the maximum KE (in eV) of the photoelectrons emitted?</p><p>(b) Estimate the number of photoelectrons emitted per second.</p><p class=\"study-figure\"><img src=\"assets/textbook-examples/media/1388b4e1467b4d5fe9d33464.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width:184.9px\"/></p>","answer":"<p>(a) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>K</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>a</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>x</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow></mrow></math> × 1.8 V = 1.8 eV</p><p>(b) Saturated current = 2.8 × 10<sup>−6</sup> A</p><p>In other words, 2.8 × 10<sup>−6</sup> C of charge is emitted in each second.</p><p>Number of photoelectrons emitted per second</p><p>= <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>2</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>8</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext> </mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>×</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext> </mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>1</mtext></mr